cade's.\n39\tP2-4. .claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/decisions_cli.py:195-202, together with fact_canonical.py:147 and fact_state.py:23/38/54. The new veto_triggered emit, keyed on reason_code, reads only the final decision. When the fact gate in ENFORCE mode, or the ADR-175 citation pilot, replaces a bash_indirect_* block, the new Decision is built without reason_code. Scenario: on those paths no veto_triggered event with the indirect reason code is written; only the fact-gate or citation events are. This affects audit records only; the block decision is unchanged. Minimal fix: pass reason_code=decision.reason_code into the replacement Decision constructors.\n40\t\n41\tVERDICT: GO The fragments in this payload match the pre-split code wherever I compared them, keep the fail-open and fail-closed directions, stay stdlib-only and Python 3.9-compatible, are covered by the condition-5 kernel rows, and make no declared condition false; the only findings are four P2 follow-ups.\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4310e5bd-b4b6-4a4e-b8bd-71d847027e9a","uuid":"a1f067bb-0136-4b2c-9a96-1d0039de6f85","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:05:38.347Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-04.verdict.txt","content":"PAYLOAD 4/32. Files: the new fragments under .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_log_parts (paths_skills.py, rotation_storage.py), .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_query/* (9 files) and .claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts (__init__.py, decisions_cli.py, fact_canonical.py, fact_state.py). I read them together with the facades that load them (audit_log.py:305-329, check_bash_safety.py:1-42, .claude/scripts/audit-query.py:174-385). I compared them with the pre-split staged copies in .claude/plans/PLAN-182/staged-w1 and with the PLAN-194 auditrace patch.\n\nFINDINGS\nP0: none.\nP1: none.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED\n1. Moved code. These checks mat