udit_log.py does.\nP2-3. .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_query/labeling.py:19 and :51; parsing.py, queries.py, reporting.py, reporting_health.py. These are importable modules, but they are correct only once audit-query.py rebinds them.\n- parsing.py, queries.py, reporting.py and reporting_health.py use names they never define: _BY_DOMAIN_DEFAULT_WINDOW_DAYS, _LABEL_VALID_*, default_errors_path, _parse_since_arg, cmd_compliance, cmd_metrics. Called directly, they raise NameError.\n- labeling's own _LABEL_STORE_PATH points at .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_query/audit-log-labels.jsonl. Its sys.path insert resolves to .claude/hooks/_lib/hooks/_lib, so audit_hmac fails to import and the fixed fallback key is used.\n- Scenario: a future direct \"from _lib._audit_query import labeling; labeling.cmd_label(...)\" writes inside _lib, and the resulting label chain fails verification against the real key. No such caller exists today; audit-query.py is the only importer.\n- Minimal fix: pass the store path and hooks directory explicitly, or add a guard that raises when the function's globals are not the facade's.\nP2-4. .claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/decisions_cli.py:195-202, together with fact_canonical.py:147 and fact_state.py:23/38/54. The new veto_triggered emit, keyed on reason_code, reads only the final decision. When the fact gate in ENFORCE mode, or the ADR-175 citation pilot, replaces a bash_indirect_* block, the new Decision is built without reason_code. Scenario: on those paths no veto_triggered event with the indirect reason code is written; only the fact-gate or citation events are. This affects audit records only; the block decision is unchanged. Minimal fix: pass reason_code=decision.reason_code into the replacement Decision constructors.\n\nVERDICT: GO The fragments in this payload match the pre-split code wherever I compared them, keep the fail-open and fail-closed directions, stay stdlib-only and Python 3.9-compatible, are covered by the condition-5 kernel rows, a